concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-8a-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "8A(2) Consultation with Gene Technology Regulator"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-8a-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The NRA must consult the Gene Technology Regulator in accordance with this section for the purposes of the following:  (a) deciding whether to grant an application under the Code in relation to any of the following:  (i) approval of the active constituent;  (ii) registration of the chemical product;  (iii) approval of a label for containers for the chemical product;  (b) deciding whether to grant an application under the Code in relation to a variation of any of the following:  Schedule 1  Consequential amendments  (i) the approval of the active constituent;  (ii) the registration of the chemical product;  (iii) the approval of a label for containers for the chemical product;  if the variation may affect the GM product;  (c) reconsidering any of the following:  (i) the approval of the active constituent;  (ii) the registration of the chemical product;  (iii) the approval of a label for containers for the chemical product;  (d) deciding whether to issue a permit in respect of:  (i) the active constituent; or  (ii) the chemical product." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The NRA must consult the Gene Technology Regulator in accordance with this section for the purposes of the following:  (a) deciding whether to grant an application under the Code in relation to any of the following:  (i) approval of the active constituent;  (ii) registration of the chemical product;  (iii) approval of a label for containers for the chemical product;  (b) deciding whether to grant an application under the Code in relation to a variation of any of the following:  Schedule 1  Consequential amendments  (i) the approval of the active constituent;  (ii) the registration of the chemical product;  (iii) the approval of a label for containers for the chemical product;  if the variation may affect the GM product;  (c) reconsidering any of the following:  (i) the approval of the active constituent;  (ii) the registration of the chemical product;  (iii) the approval of a label for containers for the chemical product;  (d) deciding whether to issue a permit in respect of:  (i) the active constituent; or  (ii) the chemical product."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ce9f02af54e6364072f972a135c07eff6143388a08b9cfc656f7f1631e06666c" ;
    values:partOf concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-8a ;
    cof:pageNumber "7"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Consultation with Gene Technology Regulator for certain decisions and actions" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
